// Benchmark 9 (`docs/rfc.md` §7.8): Conflicting jurisdictions, superior entrenchment, and explicit unresolved priority.
//! explore: 1
#require "../lib/jurisdiction.charter".

Fact realm Identified by TreatyUnion, MemberStateA, MemberStateB.
Fact firm Identified by CarrierX.
Fact rule-topic Identified by DataPortability, LocalTariff.

Use jurisdiction(realm, firm, rule-topic) As jx.

+jx-subordinate-to(MemberStateA, TreatyUnion).
+jx-superior-entrenched(TreatyUnion, DataPortability).
+jx-nexus(TreatyUnion, CarrierX).
+jx-nexus(MemberStateA, CarrierX).
+jx-nexus(MemberStateB, CarrierX).

Scenario treaty-supremacy-and-peer-conflict {
  ?!valid jx-enact-prohibition(MemberStateA, CarrierX, DataPortability).
  jx-enact-mandate(MemberStateA, CarrierX, LocalTariff).
  jx-enact-prohibition(MemberStateB, CarrierX, LocalTariff).
  ?jx-contested-jurisdiction(CarrierX, LocalTariff).
}
